post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

picom-motion-git is picom with two plugins: ws-direction (workspace transitions) and
win-cause (window animations, i3 only). They do nothing until picom.conf names them.
The lines for ~/.config/picom/picom.conf and your i3 config are on

  https://jornc.github.io/picom-motion/install.html

from "4. picom.conf" on. Steps 1 to 3 there build what this package installed.

The styles are in /etc/xdg/picom/include/. To change one, copy it to
~/.config/picom/include/ with the same path: picom looks there first.

This picom is a fork that stages changes offered to picom. Report problems with it at
https://github.com/JornC/picom-motion/issues, not to picom. Back to picom:

  sudo pacman -S picom
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'

picom reloads its config by itself, but not its own program: restart picom to run
this version.
EOF
}
